WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.220
Today, we had a singing test in our elective music class.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.720
I was so nervous.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.230
There's some kind of dark aura...

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:24.610
Stupid music, stupid music, stupid music...

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.240
I'm tone deaf!

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.410
Your singing was great, Aya.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.870
There was something really "Aya" about it!

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.660
It was an Aya-chan voice.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.460
It made me think, "That's our Aya!"

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.410
<i>The</i> Ayaya!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.120
That's definitely not praise!

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:42.460
Youko, you seemed to be having fun, singing so loudly.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.580
Really?

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.840
Thanks.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.010
Shino, your voice was like a pipe organ.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.470
You're talking about a human!

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.140
Everyone was smiling while you sang, Alice.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.890
<i>Moon, moon...</i>

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:07.240
<i>We gazed upon the round snow globe together.</i>

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.660
<i>If it snows today...</i>

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:13.660
I know!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.790
Why don't you record yourself and broadcast it across the nation?

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.370
You'll bring smiles to the world!

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.830
Please don't!

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.460
Karen, you were so good.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.510
I wasn't <i>that</i> good.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.800
Well, your Japanese was a little off in a few places.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.850
I'd like to hear you and Alice do a duet.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.430
Sure.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.310
I'll sing the soprano part.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:38.040
What?

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.980
But I want to be the soprano!

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.690
No, me!

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:43.740
My voice is higher!

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.860
Don't fight, you two.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.990
Now, I'll...

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.360
...clap along with you.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.240
You're not singing the alto part?

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:18.480
<i>Searching for the sigh of spring and letters of the wind,</i>

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:28.400
<i>I looked up at the beautiful sky.</i>

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:38.040
<i>Someday, even these lovely days will flutter about,</i>

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:44.040
<i>With the dignity of the cherry blossoms...</i>

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.760
The season has finally arrived.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.810
Is something special happening?

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:21.570
Yes.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.340
Around this time every year,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.810
when autumn comes, I can finally...

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.060
The fit really puts my mind at ease.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:34.820
Karasuma-sensei, you're making us feel kinda sad.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.370
That's what it means.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.700
I see.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.870
Alice, what are you writing?

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:49.960
I write down difficult Japanese words that I hear at school, so I don't forget them later.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.620
I see.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.240
You won't forget them if you write them down.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.420
Aya, what do you have in your bag?

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.610
My tracksuit.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.970
We've got P.E. next.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.680
I forgot!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.470
It's in your notes, though...

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.730
I put it somewhere I'd see it,

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.520
right next to the front door, so I wouldn't forget it!

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.810
You're pretty scatterbrained, huh?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.810
Shino, you didn't notice?

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.320
Now that you mention it,

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.610
I did think, "We have P.E. today, but Alice doesn't have her tracksuit."

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.820
You noticed and said nothing?!

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.490
But I thought she might be wearing it underneath her clothes.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.330
<i>It's not like a swimsuit.</i>

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.040
Alice, it's okay!

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.750
This is why Karasu-chan's tracksuits exist!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.290
What?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.630
B-But she's the teacher...

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.130
It's all right.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.300
The design hasn't changed much.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.310
No one will know.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.010
But, Sensei...

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.140
She let me borrow her jacket, but I don't have any pants.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.440
It's okay, you don't need any.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.270
It's like you're wearing nothing but a shirt.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.190
Yes, it doesn't look strange at all.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:55.830
What?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.300
That's not okay!

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.250
I have my summer shorts.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.320
That's it!

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.620
Gather 'round, everyone.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.830
Okay.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.080
I'm s-so cold.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.340
P.E. should just disappear from this world.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.420
What are you talking about?

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.090
Don't just sit and watch.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.100
Ow! Ow!

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.140
Stop!

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.100
Don't make such weird noises.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.010
I'm not very flexible.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.560
Don't push so hard.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:35.980
Ow! Ow!

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.630
I give up!

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.400
This isn't a stretching exercise!

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.450
Shut up.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.700
One thousand meters?

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.870
Why do we have to run that far?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.120
Does something good happen if we do?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.790
You're as slow as you look, Aya.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.460
I'm going on ahead.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:01.970
C-Come to think of it, where are Shino and Alice?

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.840
They're so slow!

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:05.930
Shino?

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:08.560
She's slow, but she's not short of breath.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:10.930
Shino.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.060
Ah, Aya-chan.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.020
If you can afford to go faster,

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.820
you'll tire less if you run at your own pace.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.900
No, I can't run any faster than this.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.320
This is my top speed.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:22.280
What?

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.610
But you don't look even the least bit tired.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.450
I suppose I'm not...

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.700
I could keep running for two or three hours.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.220
Why do you have so much stamina?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.000
S-Shino.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:34.710
Yes?

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.180
Oh no, Aya-chan!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.090
It's Alice!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.340
She's trying to tell us something in English.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.260
O-One more, please?

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.100
N-No, not that...

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:51.770
I know.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.060
I'll teach you an incantation to reduce your fatigue.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:55.690
What?

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:56.810
Something like that exists?

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:02.570
I hear athletic clubs saying it all the time, so it must be effective.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.490
Let's see... What was it?

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.320
Fi... fi...

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.930
Oh, "fluffy".

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.120
That's it.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.160
I think they say "fluffy".

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.910
Fluffy?

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.080
Repeat it after me.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:23.670
Fluffy.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.430
How can you be so tired?

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.510
Alice, are you okay?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:37.230
I think this is an appropriate time to use this word.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:39.690
Does this work?

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.980
Yeah, more or less.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.870
Does anyone know the answer to this question?

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.750
What?!

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:06.670
Whenever that happens, you're supposed to raise your hand even if you don't know the answer.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:07.800
That can't be right!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.090
What if you don't know the answer?

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.600
It's all right.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.270
If you don't, it's your opportunity to make a joke!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.060
Answer the question!

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.110
It's time for lunch, but I ate it earlier,

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.570
and now, I have nothing.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.330
Can I have a piece of fried chicken?

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.410
You're hopeless.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.910
Open wide!

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:41.920
It's good.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.880
What are you doing?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:52.930
Lunch time!

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.560
'Scuse me!

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:59.190
By the way, Karen, you're always late coming over here.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.770
What are you normally doing?

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:04.270
I eat lunch with the girls in my class first.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.030
What are all these buns and snacks for, then?

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:11.860
People give fruit and snacks to Jizo statues, yes?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:12.820
You mean offerings?

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.580
<i>Karen-chan, you can have this.</i>

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.370
<i>I made it myself.</i>

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.330
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:21.990
<i>You're welcome.</i>

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.960
It's just like that.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:28.210
In other words, they're all gifts from other people?!

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:31.680
I wonder if it feels like feeding a cute little animal.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.260
You could show some restraint.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:35.220
What?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:38.500
Everyone so nice, and I so happy!

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.850
Everybody happy!

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:40.880
Hey!

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.100
Your broken Japanese sounds suspiciously fake.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:46.520
Karen, have you put on weight since you came to Japan?

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:47.150
What?!

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:49.240
I-Impossible!

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:52.910
If you eat that much every day, you'll get fat.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.580
Karen, here.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.370
What?

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.130
You need to go on a diet.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.760
I've never dieted before.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:15.010
Maybe someone can give us some ideas...

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:20.680
Sensei?

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.480
You mustn't push yourself too hard when you diet.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.410
Whenever you remember, try twisting your body,

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.940
or lifting your legs higher when you walk.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.040
I see.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.740
That sounds easy.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.910
But your butt's a bit on the big side, Sensei.

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:38.370
What?!

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.200
Hey, Karen, that was rude.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.290
It's called "birthing hips".

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.790
You should use that from now on.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:46.790
I'm not sure that's any better...

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:51.050
Youko, you eat a lot, but your figure never changes.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:54.090
That's because I go running nearly every day.

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.430
You just have to exercise as much as you eat.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.720
Then, I'll run with you, Youko.

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.820
How far do you run?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.190
About ten kilometres, I think.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.690
I'll run about ten centimetres, then.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.300
That's pointless!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:14.200
Girls should be a little chubby.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:17.160
That's what my sister told me.

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:21.450
<i>I want to be like you.</i>

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:22.300
<i>What?</i>

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.160
<i>You're fine the way you are.</i>

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.880
<i>Your rounded and absent-minded qualities are plenty cute.</i>

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.550
She said that I'd look like an emaciated capybara if I lost any weight.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:38.550
Does that mean you're a capybara in the first place?

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.930
The first important thing is to know your current weight.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.810
I'll measure mine first.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:52.820
Huh?

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.700
Is this scale broken?

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.360
No, I don't think so.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.730
It must be because of my clothes, then.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:01.570
That's it.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:02.900
That must be it.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:03.950
Face reality!

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.540
And don't take off your clothes!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.540
My weight hasn't changed.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:12.500
Really?

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.010
It's your fault for calling me fat, Alice.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.130
How much do you weigh?

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:18.820
What?

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:20.480
You want me to tell you?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.510
How embarrassing.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.640
You can whisper it to me.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:31.400
<i>I'm way heavier!</i>

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.530
Aya, where are you going?

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:40.070
So I can keep accepting food from
everyone just like I've been doing, right?

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:41.990
You really shouldn't.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:45.330
Restraint embodies the Japanese spirit.

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.870
You should learn from the Japanese.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:50.250
Also, just eating snacks all the time isn't healthy.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:53.180
I'll make you a packed lunch tomorrow.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.190
I'd like to eat a packed lunch made by you, too.

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:01.300
I-I'll do my best for you, Shinobu!

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.910
Leave it to me!

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.560
What about me?

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:12.020
You're waking up at the same time as my mother, right?

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:12.980
Yes.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:14.070
Will you be able to get up?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.190
I'll be fine.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.920
She wakes up at five every morning.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.410
This'll be fine...

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.330
<i>She's suddenly slacking off?!</i>

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.580
Good merrning...

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.420
Good morning, Alice-chan... merrning?

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.080
<i>I know!</i>

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.850
<i>I'll make the rice look like the Union Jack.</i>

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.350
<i>What on Earth is she making?</i>

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:56.980
Alice, we have to go to school soon.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.360
Wait just three more minutes.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:05.280
Alice made my lunch today.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.950
Is it some kind of character lunch?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:16.790
I couldn't make the blue parts, but it's supposed to be the Union-

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:17.940
Rice.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:18.880
Rice?

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:20.260
Rice!

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.010
She wrote "rice" on the rice!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.010
It's autumn.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:30.930
When you think of autumn...

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.140
I think of the arts.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.190
Appetites.

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.820
Coloured leaves.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.460
Sports.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.860
How 'bout you, Ayaya?

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.110
Autumn is for studying.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:41.480
What?

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.150
You're so serious, Aya.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.670
Think of something that's more fun.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.610
Our exams start next week.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.030
Are you going to be all right?

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:49.870
What?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.340
Oh, no!

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.370
I forgot all about it.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.040
This isn't good.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.330
I like tests.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:57.860
What?

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:58.630
Why?

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.500
I thought you were like me.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.880
I love testing season.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.550
The quiet classrooms.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.640
The scratching of pens.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.220
It's just perfect for naps!

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.980
You're supposed to answer questions!

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.810
I like tests, too.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:19.360
Shino quizzes me before tests.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.400
Right?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.300
Shino, you can't afford to do that.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.240
You failed last time.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.950
How do you know that?

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:31.700
It appears the time for me to teach you my motto has finally arrived.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:38.490
It's "Que sera sera, whatever will be, will be."

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:44.420
Your "whatever" isn't "being" very well.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:52.390
I lose consciousness when I study.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.140
That's because you're falling asleep.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.270
Don't go to sleep.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:02.230
Just once, I'd like to score in the 90s like Alice.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.530
Shino.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:08.160
Okay, I'll help you!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.490
You can copy off my answer sheet!

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.700
Alice.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.900
You can't do that!

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.660
Study!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.800
Sensei, I brought the class journal.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.170
Okay.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.840
Oomiya-san, how is your studying going?

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.470
It's coming along.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:35.980
Sensei, I can become an interpreter in the future, right?

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.940
I-I believe in you!

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.690
Sensei, are you crying?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.320
What's going to be on the test?

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.750
You're starting there?

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.950
Shino, welcome back.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:53.740
Is something wrong?

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:57.370
Alice, please teach me English.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:59.670
Shino's suddenly feeling inspired to study!

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.520
I've never seen her like this before!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.240
Shino!

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.380
More like...

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.730
Who are you?!

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.220
Good morning, everyone.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.600
Morning, Alice.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:16.390
G'mo'ning!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.890
Hello, goodbye... Que sera sera...

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:21.230
I-Is she okay?

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:23.980
It's time for her to show us the fruits of her labour.

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:26.150
You can do it, Shino.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:28.530
Je t'aime.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:31.320
<i>It's... French...</i>

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.450
<i>No good can come of this.</i>

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:36.740
You can do it, Shino.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.260
Yes.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.870
I did everything I could.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.040
I feel like I can do anything right now.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.630
It's all thanks to you, Alice.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:51.510
<i>S-Shino's not acting like herself.</i>

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:55.350
There's a blonde princess over there!

00:18:58.140 --> 00:18:59.060
Huh?

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:03.020
I forgot the words I learned.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.440
I-I'm sorry, Shino!

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:11.070
Youko, it doesn't look like you're studying much.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:12.490
Are you okay?

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:14.240
I studied at home,

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:17.620
but there's a limit to how much I can memorise.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:22.290
That's why I decided to look inside your mind for the answers!

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.370
It's a great idea!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.210
Y-You can do that?

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:28.170
It's all about spirit.

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:29.670
Begin.

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.340
<i>I can feel her eyes on me.</i>

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:37.940
<i>Don't pay attention to her.</i>

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.310
<i>I need to focus.</i>

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:41.930
<i>Focus... focus...</i>

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:46.650
<i>I have no idea.</i>

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:53.360
If I get a bad grade, it'll be your fault.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.950
I should be saying that!

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.090
<i>That sound...</i>

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.680
<i>As long as you remember what you studied,</i>

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.100
<i>you should get a good grade.</i>

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:26.850
<i>You can do it, Shino.</i>

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:30.110
<i>It's your chance to restore your lost faith.</i>

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:35.550
<i>You can do it, everyone.</i>

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.580
It's over.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:46.310
I love the feeling of freedom you experience after tests.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:48.210
We have more tomorrow.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:50.670
Shino, good work.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.920
<i>Shino's a shell.</i>

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.170
It's like she aged all at once.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:00.470
Hey, she's sensitive about that.

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.810
She really did get a good grade!

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.230
Shino, that's amazing!

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:10.940
<i>She did better than me.</i>

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:14.070
Thank you, Alice.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:16.400
I've never scored so high before.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.410
No, it's all the result of your own hard work.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:23.700
I'm so happy... So happy...

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:27.480
Sensei, please don't cry.

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:01.800
I scored an 80 on my math test.

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:04.520
Shino, how did you... do...

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:13.020
Now we match!

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:16.020
Alice.

00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:19.990
She's back to her usual self.

00:23:21.820 --> 00:23:24.610
Let's study in the classroom during our exams.

00:23:24.610 --> 00:23:28.070
Aw, can't I go to the class next door?

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:30.080
If you behave yourself, I'll give you chocolate.

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:32.080
I'm going to study!

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:32.990
It feels like this...

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:35.950
See you next time! Bye!
